1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:04,950
Diffusion MRI records how water moves through the living brain.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:11,550
Mapping anatomy has usually meant a second, T1-weighted scan, registered into diffusion space.

3
00:00:12,100 --> 00:00:19,250
SlicerDDSurfer reconstructs anatomy directly from diffusion MRI, without a T1-weighted scan.

4
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:24,350
It maps microstructure, from DTI to free water, NODDI and kurtosis.

5
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:26,200
Tissue labels.

6
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:29,800
Brain regions.

7
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:33,350
White and pial surfaces,

8
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:35,722
all in native diffusion space.

9
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:41,018
Whole-brain tractography, traced in the same native space.

10
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:49,224
White-matter bundles, from the same tractogram.

11
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:54,531
And structural connectomes, built on the same anatomy.

12
00:00:55,800 --> 00:01:01,300
One 3D Slicer module, with automatic QC and a record of every run.

13
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:11,950
SlicerDDSurfer. Brain anatomy from diffusion MRI, inside 3D Slicer.
